<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Julius Sundblom</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1865">1865</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Julius Sundblom was a journalist and politician from the Åland Islands who led the movement for reunion with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> after Finnish independence. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/league-of-nations">League of Nations</a> awarded Åland to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> with guaranteed autonomy in 1921, he became the first speaker of its parliament, the Landsting, which first met in 1922, and held the post for many years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-sundblom.jpg" alt="Julius Sundblom" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mona-Mia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Julius_Sundblomi_haud.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
